Title: Run without the sandbox when started from a network drive
Origin: electron-legacy (this repo)

Started from a mapped share, a UNC path or a VirtualBox shared folder, Electron
crashes on Vista and later and runs on XP. --no-sandbox makes it run, which is
how the cause was confirmed.

A sandboxed child is started at low integrity on a restricted token, and the
network redirector does not serve that token the files the child is made of.
XP has no integrity levels. Turning UAC off does not change this: the sandbox
lowers the integrity level of its children itself.

So the browser process looks at the volume its executable is on, and if that
is a remote one, on Vista or later, adds --no-sandbox itself and logs that it
did. In ElectronMainDelegate::BasicStartupComplete, beside the existing
ELECTRON_DISABLE_SANDBOX check, which is early enough for the same reason that
one is: nothing has asked whether there is a sandbox yet. The children are
given the switch by the browser, as they are when it is typed.

GetVolumePathNameW and not the first three characters of the path, so that a
UNC path and a folder mounted from a share are both seen for what they are.

This turns a security boundary off, for launches that otherwise do not start
at all. It does nothing for an executable on a local disk.

diff --git a/electron/shell/app/electron_main_delegate.cc b/electron/shell/app/electron_main_delegate.cc
--- a/electron/shell/app/electron_main_delegate.cc
+++ b/electron/shell/app/electron_main_delegate.cc
@@ -65,7 +65,10 @@
 #endif
 
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)
+#include <windows.h>
+
 #include "base/win/win_util.h"
+#include "base/win/windows_version.h"
 #include "chrome/child/v8_crashpad_support_win.h"
 #endif
 
@@ -207,6 +210,29 @@
   if (env->HasVar(kElectronDisableSandbox))
     command_line->AppendSwitch(sandbox::policy::switches::kNoSandbox);
 
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)
+  // electron-legacy: started from a network drive -- a mapped share, a UNC
+  // path, a VirtualBox shared folder -- every sandboxed child dies at launch
+  // on Vista and later. It runs at low integrity on a restricted token, and
+  // the network redirector will not serve that token the files the child is
+  // made of. XP has no integrity levels and is not affected. Run without the
+  // sandbox there, which is what the user would have to find out to do.
+  if (IsBrowserProcess() &&
+      !command_line->HasSwitch(sandbox::policy::switches::kNoSandbox) &&
+      base::win::GetVersion() >= base::win::Version::VISTA) {
+    base::FilePath exe;
+    wchar_t volume[MAX_PATH + 1] = {};
+    if (base::PathService::Get(base::FILE_EXE, &exe) &&
+        ::GetVolumePathNameW(exe.value().c_str(), volume, MAX_PATH) &&
+        ::GetDriveTypeW(volume) == DRIVE_REMOTE) {
+      LOG(WARNING) << "Running from a network drive (" << exe.value()
+                   << "): the sandbox is disabled, as its processes cannot "
+                      "start from one.";
+      command_line->AppendSwitch(sandbox::policy::switches::kNoSandbox);
+    }
+  }
+#endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)
+
   tracing_sampler_profiler_ =
       tracing::TracingSamplerProfiler::CreateOnMainThread();
 
